Collect Haskell query counters under the connection lock even when a
maintenance test already closed the database, then dispose the agent.
Never query a closed C handle to collect this metadata.

Raise the terminal and server-start waits to 30 seconds.  The release test
build runs with debug assertions off, and the full suite on a loaded machine
routinely needs more than the upstream five seconds before the client prints.

Do not divide by zero when merging query statistics.  A query that fails
before it ever succeeds is recorded with count 0 (DB.updateQueryErrors), and
the shared per-run maps are merged once per chat (chat and agent store) over
the whole suite.  When the same failing query is seen in two examples, both
entries have count 0 and the weighted average divides by zero.  Keep the
average at 0 in that case; the failure itself is still reported through the
errs map.

